# GIBS API Contracts — ARCHIVED, NOT IMPLEMENTED

> **Status: ARCHIVED HISTORICAL MATERIAL. NOTHING HERE IS IMPLEMENTED.**
>
> These contracts describe a Vercel serverless API and a PostgreSQL database that
> **are not part of the current GIBS product and are not deployed.** No API
> endpoint exists in the current architecture. The frontend has zero `/api/`
> dependency and renders entirely from `src/lib/data.ts`.
>
> Do not read this file as a description of the current system. It is retained
> only to record what was once designed.
>
> **The implementation has since been deleted.** The `api/` tree
> (`catalogue.ts`, `programmes/[slug].ts`, `_lib/db.ts`, `_lib/shared.ts`) was
> removed on 2026-10-04: it was fully orphaned, and `pg` / `@vercel/node` were
> never installed. Every endpoint specified below no longer exists in any form.
>
> The current architecture is documented in `docs/PROGRAMME_CATALOGUE_RULES.md`
> and `docs/backend/README.md`.
>
> Do not implement any of this without a confirmed GIBS requirement, and do not
> add `pg` or `@vercel/node` to make it build.

## Base URL

- Production: `https://<domain>/api`
- Local: `http://localhost:3000/api` (via `vercel dev`)

## Authentication

All endpoints are **public**. No authentication token is required for reads or form submissions.
The serverless functions connect to PostgreSQL using the `service_role` via `GIBS_DATABASE_URL` (server-only).

## Error Envelope

All errors follow a consistent shape:

```json
{
  "error": "Human-readable message",
  "code": "MACHINE_READABLE_CODE",
  "requestId": "uuid",
  "details": "optional extra context",
  "fields": { "fieldName": "per-field error" }
}
```

---

## GET /api/catalogue

Returns the currently published catalogue year with all listed programmes and fees.

### Response (200)

```json
{
  "year": 2026,
  "catalogueYearId": "uuid",
  "programmes": [
    {
      "id": "uuid",
      "code": "GIBS-LOC-001",
      "title": "...",
      "slug": "...",
      "category": "...",
      "destination": "Local",
      "targetAudience": "...",
      "scheduleText": "...",
      "durationLabel": "...",
      "inPlantAvailable": true,
      "tagline": "...",
      "summary": "...",
      "fees": [
        { "tier": "standard", "amount": 250000, "currency": "NGN", "label": "..." }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Errors

| Status | Code | Meaning |
|--------|------|---------|
| 404 | NO_PUBLISHED_CATALOGUE | No catalogue year is currently published |
| 500 | INTERNAL_ERROR | Server error |

### Caching

`Cache-Control: public, s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=60`

---

## GET /api/programmes/:slug

Resolves a programme by its public URL slug.

### Query Parameters

| Param | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `year` | integer | No | Historical year (2000–2100). Without this, returns the current published programme. |

### Response (200)

```json
{
  "slug": "001-programme-name",
  "year": 2026,
  "resolution": "current",
  "programme": {
    "id": "uuid",
    "code": "GIBS-LOC-001",
    "title": "...",
    "category": "...",
    "destination": "...",
    "targetAudience": "...",
    "scheduleText": "...",
    "durationLabel": "...",
    "inPlantAvailable": true,
    "feeNotes": "...",
    "tagline": "...",
    "summary": "...",
    "format": [...],
    "audience": [...],
    "indicativeStructure": [...],
    "outcomes": [...],
    "faqs": [...],
    "fees": [...]
  }
}
```

### Resolution Outcomes

| `resolution` | Meaning |
|-------------|---------|
| `current` | The live published programme for this slug |
| `historical` | The programme for the explicitly requested year |

### Redirect (301)

If the slug was superseded:

```json
{ "redirect": true, "slug": "new-slug", "requestId": "uuid" }
```

`Location` header points to the new slug.

### Errors

| Status | Code | Meaning |
|--------|------|---------|
| 400 | INVALID_SLUG | Slug format is invalid |
| 400 | INVALID_YEAR | Year is not a valid integer in range |
| 404 | NOT_FOUND | No programme for this slug (or year) |

### Caching

- Current: `s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=60`
- Historical: `s-maxage=86400, stale-while-revalidate=3600`

---

## POST /api/enquiries

Submits a programme enquiry or general enquiry.

### Request Body

```json
{
  "name": "string (2-200 chars, required)",
  "email": "string (valid email, required)",
  "phone": "string (optional, max 40 chars)",
  "enquiryType": "string (one of 6 allowed types, required)",
  "message": "string (5-5000 chars, required)",
  "programmeId": "uuid (optional, must be published if provided)",
  "sourcePage": "string (optional, max 512 chars)",
  "sourcePath": "string (optional, max 512 chars)",
  "consent": true
}
```

### Allowed Enquiry Types

1. `Local Open Training Registration`
2. `Foreign Training Programmes (Kigali, Dubai, London, Houston)`
3. `Customized In-Plant Workshop Request`
4. `Institutional Partnership & Accreditation`
5. `Campus Facility Booking & Enquiries`
6. `General Administration & Registry`

### Response (201)

```json
{
  "id": "uuid",
  "requestId": "uuid",
  "message": "Enquiry received. The GIBS registry will respond to the email address provided."
}
```

### Errors

| Status | Code | Meaning |
|--------|------|---------|
| 400 | VALIDATION_ERROR | Field validation failures (with `fields` object) |
| 400 | UNKNOWN_FIELDS | Request contained unexpected fields |
| 400 | INVALID_PROGRAMME_ID | programmeId is not a valid UUID |
| 400 | PROGRAMME_NOT_FOUND | programmeId doesn't match any programme |
| 400 | PROGRAMME_NOT_PUBLISHED | Programme is not in a published catalogue |
| 409 | DUPLICATE_ENQUIRY | Same email + type submitted within 60 seconds |
| 413 | PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE | Request body exceeds 16KB |
| 429 | RATE_LIMITED | More than 10 enquiries per IP in 5 minutes |

### Security Notes

- Unknown fields are rejected, not silently ignored.
- `programmeId` is resolved server-side. Client-sent title/code/year are ignored.
- A programme-specific enquiry is never silently downgraded to a general one.
- Enquiries are not delivered by email — the API persists them for registry staff review.

---

## POST /api/subscribers

Registers interest in the GIBS executive bulletin.

### Request Body

```json
{
  "email": "string (valid email, required)",
  "consent": true
}
```

### Response (201 or 200)

```json
{
  "requestId": "uuid",
  "message": "Thank you for your interest in GIBS updates."
}
```

**Privacy**: The response is identical whether the email is new, already active, or reactivated.
The API does not reveal whether an email address is already subscribed.

### Errors

| Status | Code | Meaning |
|--------|------|---------|
| 400 | VALIDATION_ERROR | Email or consent validation failed |
| 400 | UNKNOWN_FIELDS | Request contained unexpected fields |
| 413 | PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE | Request body exceeds 4KB |
| 429 | RATE_LIMITED | More than 5 subscriptions per IP in 5 minutes |

### Security Notes

- Newsletter emails are NOT sent by this API. Delivery is not yet implemented.
- Duplicate handling is privacy-aware: no information leakage about existing subscribers.

---

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `GIBS_DATABASE_URL` | Yes | PostgreSQL connection string (service_role) |
| `GIBS_DATABASE_SSL` | No | Set to `false` to disable SSL (local dev only) |
| `GIBS_CORS_ORIGIN` | No | Allowed origin for CORS. Defaults to `*`. |

---

## Future Frontend Integration

When authorized, the frontend integration task should:

1. Add `fetch('/api/enquiries', ...)` to the contact form's `onSubmit` handler
2. Add `fetch('/api/subscribers', ...)` to the newsletter form's `handleSubmit`
3. Optionally fetch `/api/catalogue` for server-rendered programme data
4. Handle all error codes documented above
5. Display the `requestId` in error states for support reference

The frontend forms are already structured for this: validation runs client-side,
and the submission handler is a single function that currently transitions to a
mailto preparation state. Replacing that with an API call is a contained change.
